## Constraints and do-nots

- Do not alter anything in `{{SOURCE_DIR}}/`. Sources are immutable; the only permitted operation is moving a file to `{{PROCESSED_DIR}}/` after ingestion.
- Do not merge unrelated ideas. Preserve distinct {{ENTRY_NOUN_PLURAL}} even when they touch the same theme.
- Do not write long entries that summarise several ideas. One {{ENTRY_NOUN}} per file: {{ATOMICITY_RULE}}
- Do not create a new {{ENTRY_NOUN}} when an existing one should be reinforced instead: {{QUALITY_BAR}}
- Do not omit or obscure provenance. Every entry names its source in frontmatter.
- Where two sources genuinely disagree, keep both entries live and note the tension. Never silently pick a winner.
- Where a term carries two distinct meanings, create two entries with distinct tags rather than one hedged entry.
- Do not do Phase 1 (extraction), Phase 3 (writing), Phase 3.5 (formatting) or Phase 4 (verification) yourself. Those belong to the specialists. Your job during ingestion is orchestration, quality review and integration.
- Do not re-read files a `wiki-writer` has written in order to check them. Use `wiki-verifier` for existence and frontmatter, `wiki-formatter` for body format. Re-reading burns the context Phase 5 needs.
- Do not start a second batch in the same session. Ever.

## Search — {{SEARCH_CMD}}

`{{SEARCH_CMD}}` is configured as an MCP server in `.claude/settings.json`, so Claude Code loads it at session start. You can also call it from the shell. Install, collection setup and troubleshooting live in `resources/docs/04-search-setup-qmd.md`.

Collections:

| Collection | Folder | Contents |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `{{SOURCE_DIR}}` | `{{SOURCE_DIR}}/**/*.md` | Raw, immutable sources |
| `wiki` | `wiki/**/*.md` | The generated wiki |

Context string handed to the search engine: "{{DOMAIN_CONTEXT}}"

```sh
{{SEARCH_CMD}} query "a question in natural language"   # hybrid: BM25 + vector + rerank; best quality
{{SEARCH_CMD}} search "exact phrase"                    # fast keyword
{{SEARCH_CMD}} vsearch "a fuzzy idea"                   # semantic only
{{SEARCH_CMD}} get "wiki/{{ENTRY_DIR}}/some-slug.md"    # retrieve one file
{{SEARCH_CMD}} search "term" -c wiki                    # wiki only
{{SEARCH_CMD}} search "term" -c {{SOURCE_DIR}}          # raw sources only
{{SEARCH_CMD}} status                                   # collections, file counts, pending embeddings
{{SEARCH_CMD}} update                                   # re-index changed and new files
{{SEARCH_CMD}} embed                                    # generate vectors for newly indexed files
```

Re-index rules: run `{{SEARCH_CMD}} update` at session start, and again in Phase 5 after writing new pages. Run `{{SEARCH_CMD}} embed` when `status` reports pending embeddings, or after any batch that wrote ten or more files. The index is machine-local (`~/.cache/qmd/`), is not committed, and must be rebuilt on each new machine.

## Session startup checklist

1. Read `.claude/handover.md` — the immediate next task and any warning about an incomplete ingestion.
2. `{{SEARCH_CMD}} status` — confirm both collections are present and note pending embeddings.
3. `{{SEARCH_CMD}} update`, then `{{SEARCH_CMD}} embed` if `status` reported pending vectors.
4. Read `wiki/index.md` — orient to the current state and the existing slugs.
5. `grep "^## \[" wiki/log.md | head -5` — the last five things that happened.

## Standard ingestion protocol (mandatory)

Every ingestion session runs exactly these five phases, in order. Never skip a phase, never merge two, never run more than one batch per session.

| Phase | Owner | What happens |
| --- | --- | --- |
| 1 Extraction | `wiki-extractor` × N in parallel, one per source | Reads one source plus `wiki/index.md`; returns a structured extraction as text. Writes nothing. |
| 2 Quality review | Main agent (librarian) | Checks duplicates, atomicity, link accuracy, drops/merges; presents a verdict to the owner for approval. |
| 3 Writing | `wiki-writer` × N in parallel, one per 2–3 sources | Receives exact file content in its prompt and writes it verbatim. Reads nothing. |
| 3.5 Formatting | `wiki-formatter` × N in parallel, one per 5–7 {{ENTRY_NOUN_PLURAL}} | Reads freshly written entry files and reformats bodies to the house standard. Entries only, never source summaries. |
| 4 Verification | `wiki-verifier` × 1 | Bash checks: files exist, non-empty, required frontmatter present, counts match. Re-run writers on failure. |
| 5 Integration | Main agent (librarian) — cannot be delegated | Update `index.md`, prepend to `log.md`, update topic hubs, move originals to `{{PROCESSED_DIR}}/`, update `handover.md`, re-index search. |

Phase 1 prompts carry the source filename only. Phase 3 prompts carry the exact file content. Phase 3.5 prompts carry file paths only. Phase 4 gets the expected file list and counts. Full detail in `resources/docs/02-ingestion-protocol.md`.

### Batch sizing — shortest source first

Sort the backlog ascending by word count (`bash scripts/unprocessed.sh`) and take from the top. This clears quick wins early and reserves context for dense material later.

| Source length | Max batch |
| --- | --- |
| Short (< ~1,500 words) | 10 sources |
| Medium (~1,500–4,000 words) | 5–7 sources |
| Long (> ~4,000 words) | 3–4 sources |

A batch that mixes lengths uses the tier of its longest source.

### Phase 5 integration checklist

1. `wiki/index.md` — add one row per new {{ENTRY_NOUN}} and one per new source.
2. `wiki/log.md` — prepend `## [YYYY-MM-DD] ingest | <description>`, recording the reasoning as well as the result: entries dropped, merges rejected, tier chosen, tensions flagged.
3. Topic hubs — update `entries:` and `sources:` frontmatter *and* wire each new entry into the hub's prose. Create a new hub when a cluster of four or more related entries has no home.
4. Move each ingested original from `{{SOURCE_DIR}}/` to `{{PROCESSED_DIR}}/`.
5. `.claude/handover.md` — rewrite: what was done, current counts, immediate next task, recommended next batch.
6. `{{SEARCH_CMD}} update`, plus `{{SEARCH_CMD}} embed` if ten or more files were written.

### Critical rules

- Phase 5 must complete before the session ends. Start it the moment Phase 4 returns. A skipped integration is worse than a skipped ingest: the entries exist but nothing points at them.
- One batch per session. If context is running low mid-batch, stop after Phase 5 — do not begin another.
- You never read back {{ENTRY_NOUN}} or source files after they are written. Verifier and formatter do that.
- You alone edit `wiki/index.md`, `wiki/log.md`, the topic hubs and `.claude/handover.md`. Never delegate a write to those files.
- Close the session with `/end-session`.

## Wiki conventions

- **Processed means summarised.** A source is processed when `wiki/sources/{slug}.md` exists. After that, its original belongs in `{{PROCESSED_DIR}}/` (gitignored).
- **Wikilinks** use Foam syntax: `[[filename-without-extension]]`. A link may only name a slug that already exists in `wiki/index.md`. Agents invent plausible slugs; do not let them.
- **Slugs** are lower-case kebab-case, derived from the title, no dates, no numbering.
- **Frontmatter field names are fixed.** One spelling per field, no drift: `sources:` (plural) on entries, `entries_extracted:` on source summaries, `entries:` on topic hubs. Full schemas: `resources/docs/03-page-schemas.md`.
- **Tags** come from the established vocabulary — {{SEED_TAGS}} plus whatever the wiki has grown. Reuse before inventing.
- **Topic hubs are arguments, not link lists.** A hub that only lists links adds nothing over `index.md`.
- **All sources are `.md`.** Convert on arrival; mixed extensions break indexing.
- **Everything except `{{PROCESSED_DIR}}/` is committed**, including `wiki/`, `.claude/agents/`, `.claude/settings.json` and `.claude/handover.md`.

**Conflict resolution:** preserve the source material over link convenience. When an idea is ambiguous, split it into separate atomic entries with distinct tags rather than blending it.

## Gotchas that bite at ingest time

- **Curly apostrophes.** Filenames containing `'` (U+2019) cannot be opened with the Read tool. Use `find {{SOURCE_DIR}} -name "*keyword*" -print0 | xargs -0 cat`.
- **Broken web captures.** A cross-origin iframe warning in a clipped article is usually harmless — the prose survived. The reliable stub signal is that warning *plus* a word count under ~200. Check before extracting; a stub yields zero entries and that is the correct outcome.
- **Index pages are not sources.** Blog rolls, search-result pages and awesome-list READMEs have no extractable prose. Move them to `raw-index-pages/`.
- **Oversized files are not sources either.** Anything that needs chapter-level splitting goes to `raw-oversized/`, not into a batch.
- **Sweep for duplicates before ingesting.** Byte-identical captures are common; `diff` or checksum the backlog first.

The full set of hard-won failures, each with symptom and fix, is in `resources/docs/07-lessons-learned.md`. Read it before the first real batch.
